1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,835
This robot
has no pinky.

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:02,974
On purpose.

3
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:05,160
Boston Dynamics
says its engineers

4
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,520
taped their
ring and pinky

5
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:08,024
fingers together
for a day.

6
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,007
The verdict?

7
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:10,010
Leave it out.

8
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,520
Atlas’s new hand
has four digits,

9
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:14,254
but thirteen
degrees of freedom.

10
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:16,054
Independent
ways to move.

11
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:18,080
The company says
it can pinch,

12
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:18,880
turn objects,

13
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:20,167
and press
tool triggers.

14
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,560
A fifth digit
would mean

15
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:22,978
three more
actuators.

16
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:24,144
More cost.

17
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:24,981
More bulk.

18
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,192
More things
to break.

19
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:28,280
So the goal
is a useful,

20
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:29,443
reliable hand.

21
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,156
Looking human
is optional.

22
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:32,880
Apparently,
even robots

23
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:33,934
have a budget.
